  "question": {
    "text": "The number of real solutions of the equation \\(x\\left(x^2+3|x|+5|x-1|+6|x-2|\\right)=0\\) is ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo> </mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>We know that sum of all positive terms can never be zero,</p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>|</mo></math> can never be zero for any value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>,</p><p>So there is no value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> which satisfies the above equation<br/>Hence, only solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, i.e. number of solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> .</p></blockquote>"
  }
}